        "paragraph": "m"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          "Jesus answered them, “Isaiah prophesied correctly about you hypocrites, as it is written:",
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "‘These people honor Me with their lips,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "but their hearts are far from Me.",
            "poem": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They worship Me in vain;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "text": "they teach as doctrine the precepts of men.’",
            "poem": 2
          },
          {
            "noteId": 38
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break",
        "paragraph": "m"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          "What Defiles a Man"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break",
        "paragraph": "m"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          "Once again Jesus called the crowd to Him and said, “All of you, listen to Me and understand:"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          "Nothing that enters a man from the outside can defile him; but the things that come out of a man, these are what defile him.”",
          {
            "noteId": 43
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break",
        "paragraph": "m"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          "After Jesus had left the crowd and gone into the house, His disciples inquired about the parable."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break",
        "paragraph": "m"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          "“Are you still so dull?” He asked. “Do you not understand? Nothing that enters a man from the outside can defile him,"
        ]
      }
    ],
